{
  "_about": "Scenery props: non-resource world decoration. A prop has NO tap zone, NO gather radial, NO label and is never in the 'harvest' group (owner: 'Not every plant/rock/etc is a resource, the resources have the UI that is clickable and the props do not'). `collide` true means a static collider plus a TilePath-blocking footprint (boulders, rock spires, cliffs, logs, mounds); false means walk-through scenery (reeds, plume grass, ferns, flowers, lily pads, pebbles). `destroyable` false is reserved for really big cliffs/mesas/basalt columns (owner: 'most props can be destroyed except for like really big cliffs'); every other prop can be cleared by an attack or a build placement that needs the space. `density_per_ha` is an expected count per hectare of land in a biome where the kind is allowed, before the biome weight. `size_m` is the prop's largest dimension in metres: each model is uniformly scaled so its longest side falls in that range (so a wide log and a tall stump of one kind both read at the size the docs give; the model's own proportions are read from its mesh). `radius_m` is the collider/footprint radius in metres at size 2 m, scaled with the prop. `radius_m` is the collider/footprint radius at scale 1. `water` limits a kind to those tile types; `cliff` limits it to steep rock/ash ground (ISLANDGEN's CLIFF tiles once they exist). `card` is the painted 2D sprite for the kind: either a res:// PNG/WebP path, or `prop:<id>` naming a row in data/sprites2d.json (CardProp, the CARD2D follow-up). When the card exists the kind draws as a camera-facing billboard instead of its GLB; a kind with an empty `models` list and a card that does not exist yet is skipped, so the painted-art swap needs no code change. Models are candidates tried in order: a missing one is skipped, a kind with no existing model is skipped with one log line (the BIOMEASSETS job adds res://assets/nature/biome/*.glb).",
